<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Convolution</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Causal convolution</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section indices of sequence are represented by bracketed numbers.
The <em id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">causal</em> convolution between sequences <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}},\bm{\kappa}\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜿</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}},\bm{\kappa}\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> denoted as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> presented in <a href="#S3" title="3 Background ‣ LOCOST: State-Space Models for Long Document Abstractive Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\kappa}*{\bm{u}})[j]=\sum_{l=0}^{j}\kappa[j-l]u[l]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝜿</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\kappa}*{\bm{u}})[j]=\sum_{l=0}^{j}\kappa[j-l]u[l].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Convolution and DFT</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We are going to detail the link between convolution and the Discrete Fourier Transform. For that purpose, we need another tool, the <em id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">circular convolution</em>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Circular convolution.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s define <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\kappa}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜿</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\kappa}}</annotation></semantics></math> the periodized version of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> as: <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall j\in\mathbb{N},\ \tilde{\kappa}[j]=\kappa[j\bmod L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall j\in\mathbb{N},\ \tilde{\kappa}[j]=\kappa[j\bmod L]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For index <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq j\leq L-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq j\leq L-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the discrete <em id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">circular</em> convolution between <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\kappa}\circledast{\bm{u}})[j]=\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\tilde{\kappa}[j-l]u[l]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝜿</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊛</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\kappa}\circledast{\bm{u}})[j]=\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\tilde{\kappa}[j-l]u[l].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Convolution theorem.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The convolution theorem states that (the derivation consists only in permuting the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum</annotation></semantics></math> symbols):</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}\circledast{\bm{u}}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}\left(\bm{\hat{\kappa}}\odot\bm{\hat{u}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝜿</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊛</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}\circledast{\bm{u}}=\mathcal{F}^{-1}\left(\bm{\hat{\kappa}}\odot\bm{\hat{u}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{.}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">.</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{.}}</annotation></semantics></math> designates the DFT of a sequence and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> designates the element-wise multiplication.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Causal convolution with DFT.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To compute <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}*{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜿</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}*{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a DFT, a trick is to pad <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> zeros <em id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">before</em> taking their DFT. Indeed, if we replace <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> with their padded versions (hence vectors of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2L}</annotation></semantics></math>) in <a href="#A1.E6" title="In Circular convolution. ‣ A.2 Convolution and DFT ‣ Appendix A Convolution ‣ LOCOST: State-Space Models for Long Document Abstractive Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> we see immediately that it coincides with the <em id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">causal</em> convolution (<a href="#A1.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ A.1 Causal convolution ‣ Appendix A Convolution ‣ LOCOST: State-Space Models for Long Document Abstractive Summarization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). This means that using the Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) algorithm, the causal convolution can be computed in <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(L\log L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(L\log L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
