<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Computational complexity of a LOCOST layer</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Projection onto <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(LH^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(LH^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> time and <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(LH)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(LH)</annotation></semantics></math> space. Computing the SSM kernel <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}=\left({\bm{c}}^{\top}{\bm{b}},{\bm{c}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{b}},\dots,{\bm{c}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{L-1}{\bm{b}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜿</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}=\left({\bm{c}}^{\top}{\bm{b}},{\bm{c}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{b}},\dots,{\bm{c}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{L-1}{\bm{b}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(LHN)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(LHN)</annotation></semantics></math> time and space. Finally, calculating <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> convolutions in parallel with DFT takes <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(LH\log L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(LH\log L)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>State-space models implementation details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Parametrization.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We chose to follow the parametrization exposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022a</a>)</cite>.</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The multi-dimensional state-tensor<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">*</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">*</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">*</span>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  Using parameters in <math id="footnote6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> gives better expressive power to the convolution, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al. (2022a)</a></cite> for theoretical and empirical justifications.</span></span></span> <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}\in\mathbb{C}^{H\times N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}\in\mathbb{C}^{H\times N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math> is made of <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> diagonal matrices <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{h}=\diag(\bm{\lambda}_{h})\in\mathbb{C}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{h}=\diag(\bm{\lambda}_{h})\in\mathbb{C}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{H\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^{H\times N}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{h,n}=\exp\left(\Delta_{h}\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Re}}+i\Delta_{h}\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Im}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>Re</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>Im</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{h,n}=\exp\left(\Delta_{h}\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Re}}+i\Delta_{h}\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Im}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Delta}\in\mathbb{R}^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Delta}\in\mathbb{R}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is a time-scaling parameter.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=256</annotation></semantics></math>. Most work chose either <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=64</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=256</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Since increasing <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math> did only incur a negligible increase in memory consumption, we chose the latter, with the rationale that it should give more expressive power to <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initialization.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As reported in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022a</a>)</cite> (see their Table 3), SSMs with special initialization are tailored for long inputs processing. This has been experimentally confirmed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zuo et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, where they use non-trainable state-space layers to provide long-range contextualization in addition to local attention.</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Re}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>Re</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Re}}</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized to <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\dfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\dfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Im}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>Im</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{h,n}^{\mathrm{Im}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
